servings: 1 bowl
cook time: 30 minutes
prep time: 15 minutes
time required: 45 minutes
alternative_name: Maitake Mushroom Ramen (1-Pot Recipe)
ingredient_count: 9
---

Saute @garlic{3%cloves}(minced), @ginger{1/2%inch}(grated), and the white parts of @scallions{2}(diced, greens and whites separated) in @sesame oil{1%tbsp} until shiny and aromatic.

Add @maitake mushrooms{4-6%oz} and cook until they have released all their moisture and completely wilted down.

Add @shichimi togarashi or gochugaru flakes{1/2%tsp}, @mirin or sake{1/2%tbsp}, and @soy sauce{1/2%tbsp} and stir to mix.

Pour in @mushroom stock or water{2-3%cups}, cover with a #lid{}, and bring to a boil.

> If using low sodium stock or water, add 1/2-3/4 tsp salt.

When the broth begins to simmer, add @ramen noodles{1%brick} and lower the heat.

Simmer until the noodles are cooked through, then sprinkle with the green parts of scallions and serve.